This is an efficient, robust, stable and intuitive method for comparing two survival curves. In addition to providing a test for the equality of two survival curves, a robust estimator for the relative failure rate of the two arms was given.
Strengths
It is not able to handle patient-specific covariates. The estimator of the relative failure rate is inefficient when the differences are large.
Weaknesses
This remains the standard method for comparing two survival curves when there are no covariates.
